  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14226856/assets/9b922282db5fce22af7df867b36545077f7d609dc83ef97abf46d5f9814cbc3c.png)\n\nRounded to the **nearest integer**, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}} ${\\text{mi}}^{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}bc\\operatorname{sin}⁡A,\n$$\n\nwhere $∠A$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}с & =AB=36, \\\\ b & =AC=36, \\\\ m∠A & ={70}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘}=0.939\\,693,\n$$\n\nrounded to six decimal places,  we calculate the area as follows:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 36\\cdot 36\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{70}^{∘} \\\\  & =648\\cdot (0.939\\,693) \\\\  & ≈609\\,{\\text{mi}}^{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the **nearest integer**.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
